# Auto-commit web and data changes

After editing files under `docs/` (GitHub Pages site) or `data/` (DB, exports, shopping lists):

1. Run `kuchenplan export-web` if Python/DB changes affect the site snapshot.
2. Commit all related changes with a concise message focused on why.
3. Push to `origin/main` so GitHub Pages updates (`/docs` on `main`).

Do this without waiting for the user to ask, unless they explicitly said not to commit/push in that turn.
